5. Termination and Cleanup

The `delete_instances.sh` script read the saved instance IDs, requested termination, and waited until both instances terminated. It then removed `instance_ids.txt`. A final check returned no non-terminated EC2 instances in us-east-2.

6. Why Environment Files Are Excluded from Git

Environment files should be excluded from Git because they can contain credentials and configuration specific to an account or deployment. Even a private repository can expose these values through collaborators, compromised accounts, or a later change in visibility. Git also preserves file history, so deleting a sensitive file from the latest version does not remove it from earlier commits. In this lab, I kept the actual settings in a local `.env` file and shared `.env.example` with placeholders. This allows someone else to understand the required configuration without committing my environment file.

